 ## Overview
-Axis-Aligned Neighbor Smoothing is a weighted smoothing filter that averages color values along a single axis using depth, normal, and color similarity to preserve edges and reduce noise [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Smooth Gradient Estimation via Convolution](6449-smooth-gradient-estimation-and-smoothing.md) by restricting the kernel to a single axis and using feature-aware weights, and from [Non-local Approximated Gradients](6784-non-local-approximated-gradidents.md) by its strict axis-aligned locality and reliance on explicit geometric buffers [S1, unofficial].
+Axis-Aligned Neighbor Smoothing is a weighted smoothing filter that averages color values along a single axis using depth, normal, and color similarity to preserve edges and reduce noise [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Smooth Gradient Estimation via Convolution](6449-smooth-gradient-estimation-and-smoothing.md) by restricting the kernel to a single axis and using feature-aware weights, and from [Non-local Approximated Gradients](6784-non-local-approximated-gradients.md) by its strict axis-aligned locality and reliance on explicit geometric buffers [S1, unofficial].
 
